@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.3
@changelog
  - Codename: Where we're going we don't need no codenames
  - SSL plug-ins follow their tracks: after inserting or moving tracks, gate GR (UC1, UF8, UF1), the UF1 EQ curve and meter instance, and the HQ and A/B switches stay on the plug-in's own track. They used to shift until the project was reloaded.
  - Project tabs: each open tab keeps its own Selection Sets and recalled slot, Focus Set, Parameter Groups, Sticky Pot pins and favourite memory. Saving a project from another tab no longer empties them.
  - Settings, About: the Windows USB driver and the Linux udev rule are back, with Install and Uninstall, plus Logs. Since v0.6.1 they were hidden.
  - RME side-car (macOS): a transport key with a TotalMix action in ORC shows that action on its lamp, in ORC's colours; soft-key colours from ORC show too. Needs ORC 1.1.0.
  - Known issue: Windows 11 with Smart App Control on refuses to load the unsigned extension ("Bad Image"). Turning Smart App Control off lets it load.
